# AI Prompt And Schema Safety

- AI prompt changes are logic changes. Treat edits to prompts, model names, temperatures, response schemas, and post-processing as behavior changes.
- Flag any change to model name, temperature, structured output schema, or parsing assumptions in the task summary.
- For JSON schema changes, review every downstream consumer: parsing code, storage, UI/admin display, logs, scripts, and fallback handling.
- Preserve Russian coach and athlete tone unless the task explicitly calls for tone work. Do not let wording drift accidentally.
- Never introduce automatic AI-generated athlete-facing messages without coach approval.
- If AI is used for classification or drafting, deterministic safety gates and explicit approval paths remain primary.
- When a prompt or schema changes, include before/after notes, compatibility risks, and what manual QA proves the change is safe.
